From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:51:37 -0700
Subject: Improve memory allocation failure handling in OpenJPEG

Propagate opj_malloc() failure in opj_copy_image_header() to the
callers, so they can also fail early instead of continuing after the
memory allocation failure.

Credit to the bug reporter for providing this patch.

Bug: 574061024
Change-Id: Ifb53b384f4c0f0386794a76b1ff46e779e6849b7
Reviewed-on: https://pdfium-review.googlesource.com/c/pdfium/+/161130
Commit-Queue: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Tom Sepez <tsepez@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
The upstream change also adds third_party/libopenjpeg/0053-opj_copy_image_header.patch,
PDFium's record of the OpenJPEG source edits. That file is left out here because
its blank unified-diff context lines are trailing whitespace that Electron's
patch lint rejects; the image.c/image.h/j2k.c source changes it records are
applied in full, and the README.pdfium entry listing it is kept.

